  "Question": "Is a triangle with side lengths 5, 12, and 13 a right triangle?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "No, because \\(5^2+13^2\\ne12^2\\).",
    "B": "Yes, because \\(5^2+12^2=13^2\\).",
    "C": "Yes, because \\(5+12>13\\)."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The longest side is 13, and \\(5^2+12^2=25+144=169=13^2\\). By the converse of the Pythagorean theorem, it is a right triangle.",
